            }
          ],
          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch fixes a memory allocation bug in the Linux kernel's mempolicy module by taking a cpuset cookie around the count of nodes to be allocated from. The bug occurs when a concurrent cpuset rebind can cause a torn read of the nodemask, leading to an empty mask and incorrect allocation. The patch introduces a retry mechanism to ensure that the nodemask is valid before proceeding with the allocation. This fix has been measured to reduce zero counts by 87% in a 72-node VM.",
